  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load the past week of USGS earthquakes in the browser, pick a region, and read off live Gutenberg-Richter b-value with bootstrap range, magnitude of completeness, Omori-Utsu aftershock decay, Poisson-flagged busy hours, depth-vs-magnitude patterns and a running log of catalog revisions. Data used in the run: public. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
